IMPORT prelude

-- Northwest Territories Social Assistance Act, R.S.N.W.T. 1988, c.S-10, with the two regulations made under ss 16 and 17
-- that set who gets income assistance and how much:
--   the Income Assistance Regulations, R-038-2024 ("IA Regulations": the general stream), and
--   the Income Assistance for Seniors and Persons with Disabilities Regulations, R-037-2024 ("SPD Regulations": the stream
--   for a person 60 or over or with a disability determined by the Director, and their spouse).
-- Encoded: which stream; eligibility (IA ss 3, 3.1; SPD ss 4, 4.1); person in need (IA s 2; SPD s 3); the periods of
-- ineligibility (IA ss 4, 5; SPD ss 5, 6); the IA monthly income test (IA s 22); the SPD net annual income test (SPD s 22);
-- the maximum basic and room and board benefits (both Schedules), with the actual shelter, fuel and utility costs; the
-- budget deficit; the right to appeal (Act s 8).
--
-- SEAT: the applicant for or recipient of income assistance. "Which program do I apply under? Am I eligible? Am I a person
-- in need? How much can I get each month? What must I report, and by when? Can I appeal?" The Director and the Social
-- Welfare Officer appear only as what they must or may do for that person; their determinations (a disability, an
-- inadequate surplus, the shelter costs approved) are inputs.
--
-- Edition: the Act consolidated to 2018-11-21 (../../registers/source-bundle/social-assistance.a.2018-11-21.txt); the IA
-- Regulations consolidated to 2026-07-06 (../../../income-assistance-regulations/registers/source-bundle/
-- social-assistance.r1.2026-07-06.txt); the SPD Regulations consolidated to 2026-07-06
-- (../../../income-assistance-for-seniors-and-persons-with-disabilities-regulations/registers/source-bundle/
-- social-assistance.r5.2026-07-06.txt). English version; the French is equally authoritative.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the amounts left to "the direction of the Director" (the bridge benefit, child care, emergency assistance,
-- education and training allowances, minimal assistance under s 16(2)), which are not in the regulations; the tuition
-- and book allowances (set by reference to the Student Financial Assistance Regulations, not deposited); welfare services
-- (Act s 5(2)); a family of more than three adults (the tables stop at three: `not covered`).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the applicant's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Northwest Territories income assistance -- Social Assistance Act and its two regulations`

§§ `Questions this encoding does not cover`

DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    `the benefit tables give amounts for one, two or three adults only`
    `a family needs at least one adult or senior to apply`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH A TYPE
DECLARE `Answer` a IS ONE OF
    `answered`    HAS `the answer` IS AN a
    `not covered` HAS `because`    IS A `Why not covered`

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` x y MEANS IF x AT MOST y THEN x ELSE y

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` x y MEANS IF x AT LEAST y THEN x ELSE y

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`nil if negative` x MEANS `the greater of` 0 x

§§ `Communities and zones`

-- IA Regulations, Schedule, item 1: Zones A to F "means any of the following communities and their surrounding areas".
-- The SPD Regulations' tables are by community, the same 34 communities. The SPD tables spell two names differently
-- ("Délîne" in the basic benefit table, "Kátł’odeeche (Hay River Reserve)" in the room and board table); they are read as
-- the same communities (NOTES.md finding 9).
DECLARE `Zone` IS ONE OF `Zone A`, `Zone B`, `Zone C`, `Zone D`, `Zone E`, `Zone F`

-- The 34 communities named in the two Schedules (IA spelling).
DECLARE `Community` IS ONE OF
    `Colville Lake`
    `Délînê`
    `Fort Good Hope`
    `Norman Wells`
    `Tulita`
    `Aklavik`
    `Inuvik`
    `Paulatuk`
    `Sachs Harbour`
    `Tsiigehtchic`
    `Tuktoyaktuk`
    `Ulukhaktok`
    `Fort McPherson`
    `Fort Liard`
    `Fort Providence`
    `Fort Simpson`
    `Wrigley`
    `Jean Marie River`
    `Kakisa`
    `Nahanni Butte`
    `Sambaa K’e`
    `Behchokö`
    `Gamètì`
    `Łutselk’e`
    `Wekweèktì`
    `Whatì`
    `Enterprise`
    `Fort Resolution`
    `Fort Smith`
    `Hay River`
    `Kátł’odeeche First Nation`
    `Dettah`
    `Ndilô`
    `Yellowknife`

-- IA Schedule item 1: the zone of each community.
GIVEN `community` IS A `Community`
GIVETH A `Zone`
`the Schedule zone of` `community` MEANS
    CONSIDER `community`
    WHEN `Colville Lake` THEN `Zone A`
    WHEN `Délînê` THEN `Zone A`
    WHEN `Fort Good Hope` THEN `Zone A`
    WHEN `Norman Wells` THEN `Zone A`
    WHEN `Tulita` THEN `Zone A`
    WHEN `Aklavik` THEN `Zone B`
    WHEN `Inuvik` THEN `Zone B`
    WHEN `Paulatuk` THEN `Zone B`
    WHEN `Sachs Harbour` THEN `Zone B`
    WHEN `Tsiigehtchic` THEN `Zone B`
    WHEN `Tuktoyaktuk` THEN `Zone B`
    WHEN `Ulukhaktok` THEN `Zone B`
    WHEN `Fort McPherson` THEN `Zone B`
    WHEN `Fort Liard` THEN `Zone C`
    WHEN `Fort Providence` THEN `Zone C`
    WHEN `Fort Simpson` THEN `Zone C`
    WHEN `Wrigley` THEN `Zone C`
    WHEN `Jean Marie River` THEN `Zone C`
    WHEN `Kakisa` THEN `Zone C`
    WHEN `Nahanni Butte` THEN `Zone C`
    WHEN `Sambaa K’e` THEN `Zone C`
    WHEN `Behchokö` THEN `Zone D`
    WHEN `Gamètì` THEN `Zone D`
    WHEN `Łutselk’e` THEN `Zone D`
    WHEN `Wekweèktì` THEN `Zone D`
    WHEN `Whatì` THEN `Zone D`
    WHEN `Enterprise` THEN `Zone E`
    WHEN `Fort Resolution` THEN `Zone E`
    WHEN `Fort Smith` THEN `Zone E`
    WHEN `Hay River` THEN `Zone E`
    WHEN `Kátł’odeeche First Nation` THEN `Zone E`
    WHEN `Dettah` THEN `Zone F`
    WHEN `Ndilô` THEN `Zone F`
    WHEN `Yellowknife` THEN `Zone F`

§§ `The benefit tables`

-- Each table row gives the maximum for one, two and three adults (IA Regulations) or "adults and seniors" (SPD
-- Regulations) in the family. An "adult" is "a person who is at least 19 years of age" and a "senior" one "at least 60"
-- (s 1(1) of each).
DECLARE `Benefit row` HAS
    `one adult`    IS A NUMBER
    `two adults`   IS A NUMBER
    `three adults` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER, c IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Benefit row`
`benefit row` a b c MEANS `Benefit row` WITH `one adult` IS a, `two adults` IS b, `three adults` IS c

GIVEN `row` IS A `Benefit row`, `number of adults` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the table amount for` `row` `number of adults` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `number of adults` LESS THAN 1 THEN `not covered` `a family needs at least one adult or senior to apply`
           IF `number of adults` EQUALS 1 THEN `answered` (`row`'s `one adult`)
           IF `number of adults` EQUALS 2 THEN `answered` (`row`'s `two adults`)
           IF `number of adults` EQUALS 3 THEN `answered` (`row`'s `three adults`)
           OTHERWISE `not covered` `the benefit tables give amounts for one, two or three adults only`

-- IA Regulations, Schedule, "MAXIMUM BASIC BENEFIT TABLE": zone by number of adults ($ a month).
GIVEN `zone` IS A `Zone`
GIVETH A `Benefit row`
`the Income Assistance maximum basic benefit row` `zone` MEANS
    CONSIDER `zone`
    WHEN `Zone A` THEN `benefit row` 946 1337 1639
    WHEN `Zone B` THEN `benefit row` 885 1251 1533
    WHEN `Zone C` THEN `benefit row` 764 1081 1324
    WHEN `Zone D` THEN `benefit row` 721 1020 1249
    WHEN `Zone E` THEN `benefit row` 706 998 1222
    WHEN `Zone F` THEN `benefit row` 573 810 993

