§§ `Status in Canada (IA s 3; SPD s 4(b))`

-- IA s 3 and SPD s 4(b) (as amended by R-059-2025 and R-058-2025): a Canadian citizen; a permanent resident; a protected
-- person who has applied for permanent resident status and has been issued a social insurance number; a refugee claimant
-- whose claim has been referred to the Refugee Protection Division and not rejected, suspended, abandoned or withdrawn; or
-- a foreign national whose request under s 25(1) of the Immigration and Refugee Protection Act is pending.
DECLARE `Status in Canada` IS ONE OF
    `a Canadian citizen`
    `a permanent resident`
    `a protected person who has applied for permanent residence and has a social insurance number`
    `a refugee claimant whose referred claim is still open`
    `a foreign national with a pending section 25(1) request`
    `none of these`

GIVEN `status` IS A `Status in Canada`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the status requirement` IF NOT (`status` EQUALS `none of these`)

§§ `IA ss 4 and 5, SPD ss 5 and 6 -- how long a sanction lasts`

-- IA s 4(1), (2), (3) (a false or misleading statement) and s 5 (assistance terminated for failing to report a change),
-- and SPD ss 5 and 6, in the same words: ineligible "for the month"; for "a period of two months" if it happened before,
-- unless "(a) it has been at least 36 months since" the last time, or "(b) the applicant has not been in receipt of
-- assistance during the 12 months preceding".
GIVEN `it happened before` IS A BOOLEAN
      `months since the last time` IS A NUMBER
      `received assistance in the 12 months before` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the months of ineligibility` `it happened before` `months since the last time` `received assistance in the 12 months before` MEANS
    IF     `it happened before`
       AND `months since the last time` LESS THAN 36
       AND `received assistance in the 12 months before`
    THEN 2
    ELSE 1

§ `The Income Assistance Regulations (R-038-2024) -- the general stream`

§§ `IA ss 3 and 3.1 -- eligibility`

-- IA s 3.1(1): not eligible if (a) an SPD application is pending, or (b) the applicant "is or was a recipient under" the
-- SPD Regulations, "subject to subsection (3)": (3) eligible again if SPD assistance was terminated because the person
-- was not a person with a disability or the spouse of one. (2): not eligible during an SPD sanction period. Ss 4, 5: not
-- eligible during an IA sanction period.
GIVEN `status` IS A `Status in Canada`
      `my SPD application is still undecided` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am or was an SPD recipient` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my SPD assistance ended because I was not a person with a disability or the spouse of one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am serving an SPD or IA sanction period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is eligible under IA ss 3 and 3.1` IF
        `meets the status requirement` `status`
    AND (NOT `my SPD application is still undecided`)
    AND (    (NOT `I am or was an SPD recipient`)
         OR  `my SPD assistance ended because I was not a person with a disability or the spouse of one`)
    AND (NOT `I am serving an SPD or IA sanction period`)

§§ `IA s 22 -- monthly income`

-- IA s 22(8): allowable income "in each reporting period": "(a) $500 of earned income earned by each adult in the family;
-- (b) 25% of any earned income earned by each adult in the family in excess of the applicable amount under paragraph (a);
-- (c) $350 of unearned income." (9): money from the Canada-NWT Housing Benefit, student financial assistance, a labour
-- development program, or money the Director excludes, is not allowable income.
GIVEN `the adult's earned income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the allowable earned income of one adult` `the adult's earned income` MEANS
    `the lesser of` 500 `the adult's earned income`
    PLUS (25% TIMES `nil if negative` (`the adult's earned income` MINUS 500))

GIVEN `unearned income` IS A NUMBER, `of which money excluded by s 22(9)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the allowable unearned income` `unearned income` `of which money excluded by s 22(9)` MEANS
    `the lesser of` 350 (`nil if negative` (`unearned income` MINUS `of which money excluded by s 22(9)`))

-- IA s 22(7)(h): not counted as an asset, "money held by the applicant in a bank or other financial institution, up to a
-- maximum of twice the amount that would be required for the applicant to adequately provide for their family for one
-- month". The monthly amount is read as the family's monthly budget (the cost of its income assistance benefits) (NOTES.md
-- finding 4). The rest is unearned income under s 22(5)(r)(ii).
GIVEN `money in the bank` IS A NUMBER, `the family's monthly budget` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the bank money counted under s 22(5)(r)` `money in the bank` `the family's monthly budget` MEANS
    `nil if negative` (`money in the bank` MINUS (2 TIMES `the family's monthly budget`))

-- IA s 22(1): "monthly income" is "A + B - C", A all earned income, B all unearned income, C allowable income, of the
-- applicant and the spouse (s 22(2)). Items in s 22(6) (the Canada Child Benefit, the NWT Child Benefit, the cost of living
-- offset, RDSP money, residential school compensation, and the rest) are not income at all and are left out of A and B.
GIVEN `my earned income` IS A NUMBER
      `my spouse's earned income` IS A NUMBER
      `unearned income` IS A NUMBER
      `of which money excluded by s 22(9)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the monthly income under IA s 22(1)` `my earned income` `my spouse's earned income` `unearned income` `of which money excluded by s 22(9)` MEANS
    (`my earned income` PLUS `my spouse's earned income` PLUS `unearned income`)
    MINUS (`the allowable earned income of one adult` `my earned income`
           PLUS `the allowable earned income of one adult` `my spouse's earned income`
           PLUS `the allowable unearned income` `unearned income` `of which money excluded by s 22(9)`)

§§ `IA Schedule -- the cost of the benefits`

DECLARE `Base assistance` IS ONE OF `the basic benefit`, `the room and board benefit`

-- IA Schedule item 3(1), (3): a rental accommodation allowance "up to a maximum amount equal to the actual cost of rental
-- accommodation"; where "a subsidy is normally available, the allowance must not exceed the minimum rental rate for the
-- unit". Items 4, 5: the actual cost of fuel, and of power, water and sewage services. Whether each is provided is "in
-- accordance with the direction of the Director": the amounts are inputs, the caps computed. The SPD Schedule (items 2 to
-- 4) is in the same words.
GIVEN `my rent` IS A NUMBER
      `I live in subsidised housing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the minimum rental rate for the unit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most rental accommodation allowance` `my rent` `I live in subsidised housing` `the minimum rental rate for the unit` MEANS
    IF `I live in subsidised housing`
    THEN `the lesser of` `my rent` `the minimum rental rate for the unit`
    ELSE `my rent`

-- IA Schedule item 2: base assistance in the form of "(a) a basic benefit, not exceeding the amount prescribed in the
-- Maximum Basic Benefit Table ... corresponding to (i) the zone in which the recipient resides, and (ii) the number of
-- adults in the family; or (b) a room and board benefit" under the other table.
GIVEN `community` IS A `Community`, `form` IS A `Base assistance`, `number of adults` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the most IA base assistance` `community` `form` `number of adults` MEANS
    CONSIDER `form`
    WHEN `the basic benefit` THEN `the table amount for` (`the Income Assistance maximum basic benefit row` (`the Schedule zone of` `community`)) `number of adults`
    WHEN `the room and board benefit` THEN `the table amount for` (`the Income Assistance maximum room and board row` (`the Schedule zone of` `community`)) `number of adults`

§§ `IA s 2 -- person in need`

-- "Budget deficit" (s 1(1) of both regulations): "the amount by which the total cost of those income assistance benefits
-- that are necessary to an applicant exceeds the financial resources of the applicant".
GIVEN `the family's monthly budget` IS A NUMBER, `monthly income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the budget deficit` `the family's monthly budget` `monthly income` MEANS
    `nil if negative` (`the family's monthly budget` MINUS `monthly income`)

-- IA s 2(1): "unable to provide adequately for their family ... due to (i) an inability to obtain employment, (ii) the loss
-- of the principal family provider, (iii) illness, (iv) disability, or (v) any other cause; and (b) as a result ...,
-- (i) a budget deficit exists, or (ii) a budget surplus exists that is inadequate, as determined in accordance with the
-- direction of the Director, to provide for an unexpected situation." (2): not a person in need if "(a) a child or a mature
-- child" (under 19), "(b) incarcerated", "(c) has the means available to maintain their family adequately", "(d) refuses
-- or neglects to utilize all of the financial resources that the applicant may access, including unemployment benefits
-- and, if the applicant is 65 years of age or older, pension benefits", or "(e) is a recipient" under the SPD Regulations.
GIVEN `I cannot provide adequately for my family because of unemployment, loss of the provider, illness, disability or another cause` IS A BOOLEAN
      `budget deficit` IS A NUMBER
      `the Director finds my surplus inadequate for an unexpected situation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my age` IS A NUMBER
      `I am incarcerated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have the means to maintain my family adequately` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I refuse or neglect to use resources open to me, such as employment insurance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I refuse or neglect to draw a pension open to me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am an SPD recipient` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a person in need under IA s 2` IF
        `I cannot provide adequately for my family because of unemployment, loss of the provider, illness, disability or another cause`
    AND (   `budget deficit` GREATER THAN 0
         OR `the Director finds my surplus inadequate for an unexpected situation`)
    AND `my age` AT LEAST 19
    AND (NOT `I am incarcerated`)
    AND (NOT `I have the means to maintain my family adequately`)
    AND (NOT `I refuse or neglect to use resources open to me, such as employment insurance`)
    AND (NOT (`I refuse or neglect to draw a pension open to me` AND `my age` AT LEAST 65))
    AND (NOT `I am an SPD recipient`)

§ `The Income Assistance for Seniors and Persons with Disabilities Regulations (R-037-2024)`

§§ `SPD s 4 -- eligibility`

-- SPD s 4(a): the applicant "(i) is a senior or a person with a disability, or (ii) is the spouse of a senior or a person
-- with a disability and (A) resides with" them or "(B) has been recognized under subsection 1(2)". "Senior": at least 60.
-- "Person with a disability": a person "the Director has determined, under section 2, is a person with a disability"
-- (an input).
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER
      `the Director has determined I have a disability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I live with, or am recognised as the spouse of, a senior or person with a disability` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `falls within SPD s 4(a)` IF
        `my age` AT LEAST 60
    OR  `the Director has determined I have a disability`
    OR  `I live with, or am recognised as the spouse of, a senior or person with a disability`

-- SPD s 4.1(1): not eligible if (a) an IA application is pending, (b) the applicant "is or was a recipient" under the IA
-- Regulations "subject to subsection (3)", or (c) an Officer refused assistance under IA s 12(2) or s 14. (3): a former IA
-- recipient is eligible again on becoming a senior, a person with a disability or the spouse of one, which s 4(a)
-- already requires, so (1)(b) never bars an applicant who is within s 4(a) (NOTES.md finding 8). (2): not during an IA
-- sanction period.
GIVEN `within s 4(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `status` IS A `Status in Canada`
      `my IA application is still undecided` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an Officer refused me under IA s 12(2) or s 14` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am serving an IA or SPD sanction period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is eligible under SPD ss 4 and 4.1` IF
        `within s 4(a)`
    AND `meets the status requirement` `status`
    AND (NOT `my IA application is still undecided`)
    AND (NOT `an Officer refused me under IA s 12(2) or s 14`)
    AND (NOT `I am serving an IA or SPD sanction period`)

§§ `SPD s 22 -- net annual income`

-- SPD s 22(1): "net annual income" is "(A + E) - (B + C + D)": A "the amount reported on line 23600 of the applicant's
-- relevant notice of assessment or reassessment"; B GNWT social assistance payments; C Canada Pension Plan disability
-- benefits; D allowable income; E "any other money considered by the Director to be included as annual income". By s
-- 22(3) A, B, C and E are the applicant's and the spouse's together. (4): allowable income is "(a) if the applicant is a
-- senior or person with a disability, up to $6,000 of income received by the senior or person with a disability; (b) if
-- the applicant is a spouse, up to $6,000 of income received by the spouse." The income "received" is read as each
-- person's line 23600 amount (NOTES.md finding 6). (5): "If the allowable income ... would reduce the applicant's net
-- annual income to less than $0, only the amount sufficient to reduce the applicant's net annual income to $0 is
-- applicable."
GIVEN `my line 23600` IS A NUMBER
      `I have a spouse who is an applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my spouse's line 23600` IS A NUMBER
      `GNWT social assistance received` IS A NUMBER
      `CPP disability benefits received` IS A NUMBER
      `other money the Director includes` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the net annual income under SPD s 22(1)` `my line 23600` `I have a spouse who is an applicant` `my spouse's line 23600` `GNWT social assistance received` `CPP disability benefits received` `other money the Director includes` MEANS
    `before D` MINUS (`the lesser of` `D under s 22(4)` (`nil if negative` `before D`))
    WHERE
        `spouse's A` MEANS IF `I have a spouse who is an applicant` THEN `my spouse's line 23600` ELSE 0
        `before D` MEANS (`my line 23600` PLUS `spouse's A` PLUS `other money the Director includes`) MINUS (`GNWT social assistance received` PLUS `CPP disability benefits received`)
        `D under s 22(4)` MEANS (`the lesser of` 6000 (`nil if negative` `my line 23600`)) PLUS (`the lesser of` 6000 (`nil if negative` `spouse's A`))

§§ `SPD s 3 -- person in need`

-- SPD s 3(1): "by reason of disability or age, (a) a budget deficit exists; or (b) a budget surplus exists that is
-- inadequate, as determined in accordance with the direction of the Director, to provide for an unexpected situation."
-- (2): not a person in need if (a) a child or mature child, (b) incarcerated, (c) has the means to maintain the family
-- adequately, (d) "refuses or neglects to utilize all of the financial resources that the applicant may access, including
-- but not limited to employment or, subject to subsection (3), pension benefits", (e) "the total amount of money held in a
-- bank or other financial institution and belonging to the applicant or any member of the applicant's family, exceeds
-- $75,000", or (f) an IA recipient. (3): "An applicant is not required to access pension benefits before the applicant is
-- 65 years of age."
GIVEN `budget deficit` IS A NUMBER
      `the Director finds my surplus inadequate for an unexpected situation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my age` IS A NUMBER
      `I am incarcerated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have the means to maintain my family adequately` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I refuse or neglect to use resources open to me, such as employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I refuse or neglect to draw a pension open to me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my family's money in banks` IS A NUMBER
      `I am an IA recipient` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a person in need under SPD s 3` IF
        (   `budget deficit` GREATER THAN 0
         OR `the Director finds my surplus inadequate for an unexpected situation`)
    AND `my age` AT LEAST 19
    AND (NOT `I am incarcerated`)
    AND (NOT `I have the means to maintain my family adequately`)
    AND (NOT `I refuse or neglect to use resources open to me, such as employment`)
    AND (NOT (`I refuse or neglect to draw a pension open to me` AND `my age` AT LEAST 65))
    AND (NOT (`my family's money in banks` GREATER THAN 75000))
    AND (NOT `I am an IA recipient`)

§§ `SPD Schedule -- the cost of the benefits`

-- SPD Schedule item 1: the basic benefit or the room and board benefit, "corresponding to (i) the community in which the
-- recipient resides, and (ii) the number of adults and seniors in the family".
GIVEN `community` IS A `Community`, `form` IS A `Base assistance`, `number of adults and seniors` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Answer` NUMBER
`the most SPD base assistance` `community` `form` `number of adults and seniors` MEANS
    CONSIDER `form`
    WHEN `the basic benefit` THEN `the table amount for` (`the seniors and disabilities maximum basic benefit row` `community`) `number of adults and seniors`
    WHEN `the room and board benefit` THEN `the table amount for` (`the seniors and disabilities maximum room and board row` `community`) `number of adults and seniors`

-- The SPD test is annual (net annual income, an eligibility period from 1 July to 30 June) and the benefits monthly
-- ("provided monthly during the eligibility period", s 16(1)(b)). The regulations do not say how the two meet; the
-- encoding sets one-twelfth of the net annual income against each month's budget (NOTES.md finding 7).
GIVEN `the family's monthly budget` IS A NUMBER, `net annual income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the SPD monthly budget deficit` `the family's monthly budget` `net annual income` MEANS
    `nil if negative` (`the family's monthly budget` MINUS ((`nil if negative` `net annual income`) DIVIDED BY 12))

§ `The Social Assistance Act`

-- Act s 8(1): "An applicant for or recipient of assistance under this Act may appeal any decision made by a Social Welfare
-- Officer or the Director with respect to his or her eligibility to receive that assistance or the amount of assistance
-- paid to him or her." (2): first to the appeal committee for the place of residence; (3): then to the Appeal Board;
-- (5): the Board's decision is final, but a new application may be made on new evidence or changed circumstances.
DECLARE `Decision` IS ONE OF
    `a decision on my eligibility`
    `a decision on the amount of my assistance`
    `some other decision`

GIVEN `I am an applicant or recipient` IS A BOOLEAN, `decision` IS A `Decision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may appeal under Act s 8(1)` IF
        `I am an applicant or recipient`
    AND (NOT (`decision` EQUALS `some other decision`))
